# The image is built from source: the package, its lock and metadata, the build
# hook and the client's source. Nothing else -- no .git (the version arrives as a
# build argument), no tests, no data/, no node_modules, no built client (the web
# stage builds its own).
#
# Re-including a path from an excluded directory needs the directory
# un-excluded first, hence the pairs rather than single lines.
*
!src
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!README.md
!hatch_build.py
!web
web/node_modules
web/dist
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
